# A .semgrepignore file replaces Semgrep's built-in ignore list, so the
# built-in defaults (semgrep 1.163.0, Semgrepignore.ml) are reproduced
# verbatim below. Nothing that was scanned without this file stops being
# scanned, except the two frozen bundle directories at the end.

# Administrative folder or file used by popular version control systems
.git
.svn
_darcs
# Paths to files and folders that are typically large and ignorable
build/
vendor/
dist/
*.min.js
.env/
.tox/
# Package managers
node_modules/
.npm/
.yarn/
.venv/
_opam/
_build/
_cargo/
# Common test paths
test/
tests/
testsuite/
*_test.go

# Frozen restore bundles. Each file is a byte copy of a past live source,
# pinned by SHA-256 in the sibling manifest.json (whose own hash is pinned in
# integrity.py check_package); editing any byte, including adding a
# nosemgrep comment, fails restore verification. The live copies of this code
# under backend/core and backend/modules are still scanned.
# Frozen preserved027 snapshot of code whose live copy is scanned:
/backend/core/schema/preserved027/bundle/
# Frozen preserved029 snapshot of code whose live copy is scanned:
/backend/core/schema/preserved029/bundle/
